tuate electrolyte loss associated with diuretics.","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Formal drug-drug interaction studies have not been performed; FDA label states Acthar Gel may accentuate the electrolyte loss associated with diuretic therapy. No FDA-label CYP induction/inhibition interaction was identified.","reason":"The diuretic/electrolyte statement is supported; the stronger CYP statement lacks a named supporting source in the row.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Limited/unknown; peptide hormone mixture with adrenal cortical target effects rather than a conventional hepatic/renal ASM metabolism profile","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Limited/unknown; FDA label states pharmacokinetics of Acthar Gel have not been adequately characterized and describes Acthar Gel as a naturally sourced complex mixture of adrenocorticotropic hormone analogs and other pituitary peptides with adrenal cortical effects.","reason":"Keeps the limited/unknown classification but replaces an unsourced metabolism-profile inference with FDA-label wording.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/008372s074lbl.pdf"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"Sun 2023 melatonin supplementation add-on trial","pmid":"37909654","proposed_action":"Do not add to repository corticotropin placebo-controlled RCT links.","rationale":"The trial intervention is melatonin supplementation for infantile epileptic spasms syndrome, not repository corticotropin/ACTH.","status":"wrong_drug","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37909654/"},{"label":"Sun 2022 melatonin supplementation trial protocol","pmid":"35788069","proposed_action":"Do not add to repository corticotropin placebo-controlled RCT links.","rationale":"This is a melatonin protocol, not repository corticotropin/ACTH efficacy evidence.","s